--- body ---
## Context

Ticket [[0888]] writes four defensible one-to-one CRS purpose mappings.
`data/jetp/ontology/sector-crosswalk.csv` has one `purpose_code` per
publisher label. South African portfolio labels such as `Skills`,
`JT-Mpumalanga` and `Municipalities`, and Indonesian groups
`solar`, `bioenergy`, `energy_efficiency`, `other_dispatchable` and
`supply_chain`, can cover several purposes or grid contexts. The
author asked whether the marker system is flexible: markers can describe
policy objectives when reported, but do not determine one CRS purpose for a
broad source label. These words remain verbatim in `own_sector`.
The CIPP mirror currently has a host party but no author party in
`document-publishers.csv`, so its group words cannot yet be keyed to a
publishing authority in `sector-crosswalk`.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Review each unmapped label at the line level against the publisher's
  description and determine whether a single CRS purpose is justified.
- [ ] Establish the CIPP document's publishing party before adding a
  publisher-keyed crosswalk for its appendix groups.
- [ ] Record any source-reported policy markers on observations without
  inferring them from a portfolio label.
- [ ] Keep ambiguous labels unmapped or propose an ontology/storage change
  for author decision; do not assign a broad code silently.
